                <p rendition="#flush">N.B.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">1. To the $460,000.00 of the 1934 Budget extra provision has
                    been made for increase in operation of the Monrovia-Kakata-Saniquelli Road
                    construction, 100 additional Soldiers &amp; Officers of the Liberian Frontier
                    Force, British Postal Administration claims, etc., etc. In addition to some of
                    the increased expenditures of this year, provision will have to be made in the
                    1935 Budget for one Revenue Launch, Radio Apparatus, British Postal Claims, Road
                    Building Machinery, as well as increases in personnel for Foreign Specialists,
                    New Customs Ports of Entry, etc., etc., $500,000.00 is a minimum provision.</p>
